 "article": {
  "title": "Bees in the City",
  "topic": "环境科普（城市野生蜂多样性）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 177,
  "paras": [
   "For most of the last century, the city was considered hostile ground for bees. Concrete, traffic and pesticides seemed to leave no room. Recent surveys have overturned that assumption: in several European cities, wild bees are more diverse than in the farmland around them.",
   "The reason is flowers. Gardens, balconies, railway embankments and cemeteries provide a long, if fragmented, supply of bloom from spring to autumn. Farmland, by contrast, may offer a single crop for two weeks and then nothing.",
   "This is not an argument for moving all agriculture into cities. Cities also host fewer species overall, and their bees depend on a thin network of green spaces that can be cut by a single budget decision. A new car park can erase a decade of recovery.",
   "What cities can do is cheap and visible: plant native flowers, mow less often, leave a patch of bare ground for nesting, and stop treating every dandelion as a weed. A balcony of lavender is not a solution to biodiversity loss. It is, however, a good place to start noticing."
  ],
  "zh": "上世纪大部分时间，城市被视为蜜蜂的敌境：水泥、车流、农药似乎不留余地。但近年的调查推翻了这一假设——在欧洲几座城市，野生蜂的多样性甚至高于周边农田。原因是花：花园、阳台、铁路路基和墓园，从春到秋提供绵长（尽管破碎）的花期；而农田可能只提供两周的单一作物，然后就什么都没有。这并不是主张把农业都搬进城市：城市整体物种数仍然更少，城里的蜂依赖一张脆弱的绿地网络，一次预算决定就可能被剪断——一个新停车场就能抹掉十年的恢复。城市能做的既便宜又显眼：种本土花卉、少割草、留一块裸地给蜂筑巢、别把每株蒲公英都当杂草。一阳台薰衣草解决不了生物多样性丧失，但它是个开始留意的好地方。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Gardens, balconies, railway embankments and cemeteries provide a long, if fragmented, supply of bloom from spring to autumn.",
    "cn": "花园、阳台、铁路路基和墓地，从春到秋提供了绵长但破碎的花期供给。",
    "why": "if fragmented 是省略式让步插入语（= although it is fragmented），插在形容词后不破坏句子；supply 在此作名词，of bloom 说明供给的内容。"
   },
   {
    "en": "It is, however, a good place to start noticing.",
    "cn": "不过，它是一个开始留意的好地方。",
    "why": "however 插在 is 与表语之间，前后加逗号；start doing 表示“开始做”，比 start to do 更强调持续。"
   }
  ],
